From ab55650c7912209afebef8fa9534a29e5b3cd7b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:13:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 39/47] Translations: task panel titles as "settings", fix a
 broken Japanese term

Japanese task panel titles read "... settings" instead of the katakana
"parameters", taper and preview texts use plain words, and the generic
feature failure message is easier to read. An earlier bulk replacement
of "feature" had broken the Japanese word for Defeaturing; it is now
called "removing faces".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
